      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">A Playa Named Gus is a Jellyfin client. It connects to servers you provide and does not collect analytics, tracking data, server URLs, media metadata, or credentials for the developer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page">
    <div class="content-grid">
      <div>
        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Last updated</h2>
          <p>October 18, 2026</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
          <p>Gus stores the information needed to connect you to your own Jellyfin server:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Jellyfin server names, URLs, and IDs.</li>
            <li>Stored Jellyfin user records without passwords.</li>
            <li>Session tokens in the Apple Keychain.</li>
            <li>App preferences and local navigation state.</li>
            <li>Optional downloaded media files and metadata for the active Jellyfin server and user on iPhone, iPad, Mac, and Apple Vision Pro.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Downloaded media is stored in the app container, scoped by server and user, and excluded from device backup. Apple TV does not support persistent local downloads in Gus.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Optional private iCloud synchronization</h2>
          <p>In builds that include native Jellyfin lists, Jellyfin stores playlist and collection names, IDs, membership, playlist order and permissions. Gus keeps an account-scoped device cache and durable offline list edits until they can be sent to your selected Jellyfin server. Native list definitions and pending server edits are not synchronized through iCloud.</p>
          <p>Optional private Apple CloudKit synchronization carries supplemental Gus playlist resume positions, saved Next Up intent and activity timestamps. Legacy Gus-owned playlist records remain preserved for explicit import into Jellyfin. Synchronization is enabled when available and can be turned off in Settings → iCloud Sync.</p>
          <p>Jellyfin credentials, tokens, server URLs, signed artwork URLs, downloaded files, and imported Jellyfin watch history are excluded from CloudKit. Each device signs in to Jellyfin independently. Supplemental offline changes stay on the device until iCloud synchronization is available; pending list edits wait for Jellyfin. Changing iCloud accounts isolates supplemental Gus state. Changing Jellyfin server/user isolates cached lists and pending server edits. Signed iCloud provisioning and physical cross-device validation remain pending for this feature branch.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Data sent to Jellyfin servers</h2>
          <p>Gus sends requests to the Jellyfin server you choose, including sign-in requests, library browse and search requests, stream requests, playback progress reports, and optional download requests. That server is controlled by you or by the server operator you choose. Gus does not operate the Jellyfin server.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Optional Discover connection</h2>
          <p>In builds with Discover, you can connect a Seerr instance to search its catalog, submit movie and season requests, view request history, and approve or decline requests when authorized. Sign-in and these actions go to the Seerr operator you choose. Movie and show poster artwork may load from TMDB. The developer does not receive your Seerr searches, requests, credentials, or server address.</p>
          <p>Connection metadata is stored locally per Gus server/account. Session cookies are stored in Apple Keychain. Gus does not save passwords; Apple’s Password AutoFill may separately offer to save them at your choice. Seerr sessions are not synchronized through iCloud. Hiding Discover keeps the connection; disconnecting removes its saved local session.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Data not collected by the developer</h2>
          <p>The developer of Gus does not receive analytics, tracking identifiers, advertising identifiers, Jellyfin credentials, Jellyfin tokens, library metadata, playback history, downloaded media, or server URLs from the app.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Diagnostics</h2>
          <p>Gus uses Apple-native diagnostics for app health, such as crash counts, hangs, launch time, memory, and energy use. App-created diagnostic summaries stay on your device and do not include personal information, media titles, or server addresses.</p>
          <p>If you choose to share analytics with app developers in Apple device settings, Apple may make crash reports and aggregate metrics available through Apple's tools. That sharing is controlled by Apple and your device settings, not by Gus.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Local network</h2>
          <p>If you choose Find Local Servers, Gus uses the local network to discover Jellyfin servers. Manual server entry remains available.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>For privacy questions, open a <a href="https://github.com/eslutz/A-Playa-Named-Gus/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Issue</a> or email <a href="mailto:support@ericslutz.dev?subject=GUS%20SUPPORT">support@ericslutz.dev</a>.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

